  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Tabasco** (1 review): Reviewer singles out hearing Tabasco as a highlight of the setlist, saying the song shreds [2]\n- The set includes a tease of Scofield's \"A Go Go\" [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tabasco**: rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Spider**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-02-04.shnf** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 12 songs; 93 min; rated 3.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: A single level flutter occurs early on, possibly from a gain change on the Sonosax; Reviewer describes the sound as crisp; Reviewer finds the sound quality not brilliant [1][2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- DJ Logic played turntables and Casey Benjamin played alto sax as guests [1]\n- Reviewer says the show has an old-school feel that Soulive fans have been craving [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-02-04.shnf**: taped by Craig Davis & Pete Costello; transferred by Jon Cameron; source: Matrix: Schoeps CMC6/mk21>Sonosax & sbd (30%)>Mackie 1202>adc-20>dap1 [1]. Also: Taped with a Sonosax and adc-20, with Soulive's manager Pete Costello running the stage mics and Mackie board [1]",
